    "body": "# What does this PR do ?\n\nThe fake-host fixture inherits `BASH_ENV`. Its wrapper and Bash-based `stat` and `enroot` doubles therefore repeat the container's shell initialization even though they only simulate local commands.\n\nClear `BASH_ENV` in that fixture with one added line.\n\n**Before/after evidence**\n\n| Metric | Before | After | Evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Times Bash sourced `BASH_ENV` in the focused module | 227 | 0 | A counting probe set as `BASH_ENV` |\n| Focused module time with a 0.1-second `BASH_ENV` probe | 26.00 seconds | 2.66 seconds | One run each on one machine |\n| Focused module time with `BASH_ENV` unset | 2.80 seconds | 3.19 seconds | One run each on one machine, so this difference is noise |\n| Focused module time in a local container with `BASH_ENV=/etc/bash.bashrc` | 23.48 seconds | 2.89 seconds | One recorded local comparison |\n\nThe saving depends on how slow `BASH_ENV` is on the runner. The CI test template already exports `BASH_ENV=/dev/null` on GCP runners, so this change only helps where the image value stays set. The end-to-end CI benefit has not been measured.\n\n# Changelog\n\n- Clear `BASH_ENV` with `monkeypatch` in `fake_host`, restoring the original environment after each test.\n- Keep the wrapper execution, Bash-based `stat` and `enroot` doubles, and existing argument, path, environment, and failure assertions.\n\n# GitHub Actions CI\n\nSee the [CI section](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#-running-github-ci) in the Contributing doc for how to trigger the CI. A Nvidia developer will need to approve and trigger the CI for external contributors.\n\nValidation ran the full focused module with this PR merged onto main at `00e3730dd`, using the normal project conftest and an environment built from `uv.lock`, with and without the `BASH_ENV` probe. The assertions did not change. The probe count shows that no test in this module still sources `BASH_ENV`.\n\nNot validated: H100 and GB200 runners, and the CI container image. Upstream CI remains pending.\n\n# Before your PR is \"Ready for review\"\n\n**Pre checks**:\n\n- [x] Make sure you read and followed [Contributor guidelines](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [ ] Did you write any new necessary tests?\n- [ ] Did you add or update any necessary documentation?\n- [ ] Does the PR affect components that are optional to install? (Ex: Numba, Pynini, Apex etc)\n  - [ ] Reviewer: Does the PR have correct import guards for all optional libraries?\n\nIf you haven't finished some of the above items you can still open \"Draft\" PR.\n\n# Additional Information\n\n- Related to # (issue): N/A.\n- The unchanged tests in this module accounted for 167.87 seconds of aggregate call time across the [latest core unit-test shards](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge/actions/runs/40611624584). That is summed test time across parallel jobs, not the workflow critical path.\n",
